From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 03 Nov 2026 04:07:08 +0000
Subject: media: uapi: mpeg2: add MPEG-1 sequence and full pel flags and the MPEG-1 parsed slice format

MPEG-1 (ISO/IEC 11172-2) is the base of MPEG-2 and stateless MPEG-2
decoders can decode it, but the uAPI could not say that a bitstream is
MPEG-1. Decoding it as MPEG-2 is not correct: MPEG-1 has a different
inverse quantisation mismatch control (each coefficient made odd
instead of the parity of the sum), full pel motion vectors, and
D-pictures.

Add V4L2_MPEG2_SEQ_FLAG_MPEG1 for MPEG-1 sequences and the picture
header flags V4L2_MPEG2_PIC_FLAG_FULL_PEL_FORWARD/BACKWARD, and accept
the already defined V4L2_MPEG2_PIC_CODING_TYPE_D. Applications fill the
fields which come from the MPEG-2 extensions as ISO/IEC 13818-2 defines
them for MPEG-1 streams. Existing applications never set the new flags
and never had a way to send D-pictures, which only MPEG-1 streams have,
so nothing changes for them. Drivers without an MPEG-1 mode have to
reject the flag.

The flags alone cannot tell applications whether a decoder decodes
MPEG-1: the control framework does not check the flags of compound
controls, and the existing MPEG-2 drivers silently decode a sequence
with V4L2_MPEG2_SEQ_FLAG_MPEG1 or the full pel flags as MPEG-2, which
gives wrong pictures instead of an error that would let the application
fall back to software decoding.

Add V4L2_PIX_FMT_MPEG1_SLICE ('MG1S') for MPEG-1 parsed slice data, so
that MPEG-1 support is discovered with VIDIOC_ENUM_FMT like every other
coded format, and so that kernels and drivers without it fail at
VIDIOC_S_FMT. The format reuses the MPEG-2 sequence, picture and
quantisation controls unchanged; V4L2_MPEG2_SEQ_FLAG_MPEG1 is set with
the new format and only with it, so that the controls keep describing
the bitstream on their own.

MPEG-1 D-pictures (DC coefficients only) are rare and not every MPEG-1
capable decoder decodes them: the Rockchip VDPU2 MPEG-1 mode has no
DC-only decoding and Hantro rejects the D picture coding type. Say so
in the uAPI, and that the rejection also applies to
VIDIOC_TRY_EXT_CTRLS, so that applications can find out whether a
decoder supports D-pictures before they hand one to it, and decode or
drop them otherwise.

The format, flags and documentation are shared with the Rockchip
(Hantro VPU2) side of this uAPI: orangepi5 k15-mpeg1 commits
21d0963e021e, f22ca213f036 and f89a5beffc2e.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
--- a/include/uapi/linux/videodev2.h
+++ b/include/uapi/linux/videodev2.h
@@ -765,6 +765,7 @@
 #define V4L2_PIX_FMT_MPEG1    v4l2_fourcc('M', 'P', 'G', '1') /* MPEG-1 ES     */
 #define V4L2_PIX_FMT_MPEG2    v4l2_fourcc('M', 'P', 'G', '2') /* MPEG-2 ES     */
 #define V4L2_PIX_FMT_MPEG2_SLICE v4l2_fourcc('M', 'G', '2', 'S') /* MPEG-2 parsed slice data */
+#define V4L2_PIX_FMT_MPEG1_SLICE v4l2_fourcc('M', 'G', '1', 'S') /* MPEG-1 parsed slice data */
 #define V4L2_PIX_FMT_MPEG4    v4l2_fourcc('M', 'P', 'G', '4') /* MPEG-4 part 2 ES */
 #define V4L2_PIX_FMT_XVID     v4l2_fourcc('X', 'V', 'I', 'D') /* Xvid           */
 #define V4L2_PIX_FMT_VC1_ANNEX_G v4l2_fourcc('V', 'C', '1', 'G') /* SMPTE 421M Annex G compliant stream */
--- a/include/uapi/linux/v4l2-controls.h
+++ b/include/uapi/linux/v4l2-controls.h
@@ -2005,6 +2005,7 @@
 /* Stateless MPEG-2 controls */
 
 #define V4L2_MPEG2_SEQ_FLAG_PROGRESSIVE	0x01
+#define V4L2_MPEG2_SEQ_FLAG_MPEG1	0x02
 
 #define V4L2_CID_STATELESS_MPEG2_SEQUENCE (V4L2_CID_CODEC_STATELESS_BASE+220)
 /**
@@ -2053,6 +2054,8 @@
 #define V4L2_MPEG2_PIC_FLAG_ALT_SCAN			0x0020
 #define V4L2_MPEG2_PIC_FLAG_REPEAT_FIRST		0x0040
 #define V4L2_MPEG2_PIC_FLAG_PROGRESSIVE			0x0080
+#define V4L2_MPEG2_PIC_FLAG_FULL_PEL_FORWARD		0x0100
+#define V4L2_MPEG2_PIC_FLAG_FULL_PEL_BACKWARD		0x0200
 
 #define V4L2_CID_STATELESS_MPEG2_PICTURE (V4L2_CID_CODEC_STATELESS_BASE+221)
 /**
--- a/Documentation/userspace-api/media/v4l/pixfmt-compressed.rst
+++ b/Documentation/userspace-api/media/v4l/pixfmt-compressed.rst
@@ -129,6 +129,29 @@
 	this pixel format. The output buffer must contain the appropriate number
 	of macroblocks to decode a full corresponding frame to the matching
 	capture buffer.
+    * .. _V4L2-PIX-FMT-MPEG1-SLICE:
+
+      - ``V4L2_PIX_FMT_MPEG1_SLICE``
+      - 'MG1S'
+      - MPEG-1 parsed slice data, as extracted from the MPEG-1
+	(ISO/IEC 11172-2) bitstream. This format is adapted for stateless
+	video decoders that implement a MPEG-1 pipeline with the
+	:ref:`stateless_decoder`. It uses the controls of
+	``V4L2_PIX_FMT_MPEG2_SLICE``: metadata associated with the frame to
+	decode is required to be passed through the
+	``V4L2_CID_STATELESS_MPEG2_SEQUENCE`` and
+	``V4L2_CID_STATELESS_MPEG2_PICTURE`` controls, with
+	``V4L2_MPEG2_SEQ_FLAG_MPEG1`` set in the sequence control and the
+	fields that come from the MPEG-2 extensions filled as described for
+	that flag. Quantisation matrices can optionally be specified through
+	the ``V4L2_CID_STATELESS_MPEG2_QUANTISATION`` control.
+	See the :ref:`associated Codec Control IDs <v4l2-codec-stateless-mpeg2>`.
+	Exactly one output and one capture buffer must be provided for use with
+	this pixel format. The output buffer must contain the appropriate number
+	of macroblocks to decode a full corresponding frame to the matching
+	capture buffer. Decoders that enumerate this format decode MPEG-1
+	sequences; decoders that only enumerate ``V4L2_PIX_FMT_MPEG2_SLICE``
+	do not.
     * .. _V4L2-PIX-FMT-MPEG4:
 
       - ``V4L2_PIX_FMT_MPEG4``
--- a/Documentation/userspace-api/media/v4l/ext-ctrls-codec-stateless.rst
+++ b/Documentation/userspace-api/media/v4l/ext-ctrls-codec-stateless.rst
@@ -1317,6 +1317,19 @@
       - 0x01
       - Indication that all the frames for the sequence are progressive instead
 	of interlaced.
+    * - ``V4L2_MPEG2_SEQ_FLAG_MPEG1``
+      - 0x02
+      - The sequence is an ISO/IEC 11172-2 (MPEG-1) sequence: the inverse
+	quantisation uses the MPEG-1 mismatch control, motion vectors may be
+	full pel and pictures may be D-pictures. Applications set this flag
+	if and only if the coded format is ``V4L2_PIX_FMT_MPEG1_SLICE``;
+	drivers reject it with ``V4L2_PIX_FMT_MPEG2_SLICE``. MPEG-1 has no
+	sequence or picture extensions: applications set the fields as
+	ISO/IEC 13818-2 defines them for MPEG-1 bitstreams (chroma_format 1,
+	V4L2_MPEG2_SEQ_FLAG_PROGRESSIVE, frame pictures with
+	V4L2_MPEG2_PIC_FLAG_FRAME_PRED_DCT and V4L2_MPEG2_PIC_FLAG_PROGRESSIVE,
+	intra_dc_precision 0, both components of ``f_code[0]`` set to
+	forward_f_code and of ``f_code[1]`` to backward_f_code).
 
 .. raw:: latex
 
@@ -1366,8 +1379,12 @@
     * - __u8
       - ``picture_coding_type``
       - Picture coding type for the frame covered by the current slice
-	(V4L2_MPEG2_PIC_CODING_TYPE_I, V4L2_MPEG2_PIC_CODING_TYPE_P or
-	V4L2_MPEG2_PIC_CODING_TYPE_B).
+	(V4L2_MPEG2_PIC_CODING_TYPE_I, V4L2_MPEG2_PIC_CODING_TYPE_P,
+	V4L2_MPEG2_PIC_CODING_TYPE_B, or V4L2_MPEG2_PIC_CODING_TYPE_D in MPEG-1
+	sequences). Decoding D-pictures is optional: drivers that cannot
+	decode them reject V4L2_MPEG2_PIC_CODING_TYPE_D, also in
+	``VIDIOC_TRY_EXT_CTRLS``, which applications can use to find out
+	whether D-pictures are supported.
     * - __u8
       - ``picture_structure``
       - Picture structure (1: interlaced top field, 2: interlaced bottom field,
@@ -1415,6 +1432,16 @@
     * - ``V4L2_MPEG2_PIC_FLAG_PROGRESSIVE``
       - 0x00000080
       - Indicates whether the current frame is progressive.
+    * - ``V4L2_MPEG2_PIC_FLAG_FULL_PEL_FORWARD``
+      - 0x00000100
+      - full_pel_forward_vector of an MPEG-1 picture header: the forward
+	motion vectors are in full pel units. Only valid with
+	V4L2_MPEG2_SEQ_FLAG_MPEG1.
+    * - ``V4L2_MPEG2_PIC_FLAG_FULL_PEL_BACKWARD``
+      - 0x00000200
+      - full_pel_backward_vector of an MPEG-1 picture header: the backward
+	motion vectors are in full pel units. Only valid with
+	V4L2_MPEG2_SEQ_FLAG_MPEG1.
 
 .. raw:: latex
 
--- a/drivers/media/v4l2-core/v4l2-ioctl.c
+++ b/drivers/media/v4l2-core/v4l2-ioctl.c
@@ -1508,6 +1508,7 @@
 		case V4L2_PIX_FMT_H263:		descr = "H.263"; break;
 		case V4L2_PIX_FMT_MPEG1:	descr = "MPEG-1 ES"; break;
 		case V4L2_PIX_FMT_MPEG2:	descr = "MPEG-2 ES"; break;
+		case V4L2_PIX_FMT_MPEG1_SLICE:	descr = "MPEG-1 Parsed Slice Data"; break;
 		case V4L2_PIX_FMT_MPEG2_SLICE:	descr = "MPEG-2 Parsed Slice Data"; break;
 		case V4L2_PIX_FMT_MPEG4:	descr = "MPEG-4 Part 2 ES"; break;
 		case V4L2_PIX_FMT_XVID:		descr = "Xvid"; break;
--- a/drivers/media/v4l2-core/v4l2-ctrls-core.c
+++ b/drivers/media/v4l2-core/v4l2-ctrls-core.c
@@ -1641,6 +1641,7 @@
 		case V4L2_MPEG2_PIC_CODING_TYPE_I:
 		case V4L2_MPEG2_PIC_CODING_TYPE_P:
 		case V4L2_MPEG2_PIC_CODING_TYPE_B:
+		case V4L2_MPEG2_PIC_CODING_TYPE_D:
 			break;
 		default:
 			return -EINVAL;
